+# Native Step 5.5 PnP classification migration
+
+This opt-in protocol applies only to `inverse-problems-knot-theory-all-109-2026-10-19`, batch49, original `def-ip-pnp-ista-with-denoiser` → current `alg-ip-pnp-ista-with-denoiser`. It is separate from the original batch21 open-problem-to-example migration. Both original slots stay in the unchanged1472-subject/109-batch frontier. Aliases never confer original-slot or native-review coverage.
+
+The authentic native repeat1/u49 decision stays `confirmed_nonfatal`. Its unchanged physical review, unresolved blocker, original assignment and report stay historical. Root separately repairs the classification. No old Luna or Sol judgment, old native review, helper creation, certificate row or owner receipt becomes current algorithm review credit.
+
+## Boundary and source candidates
+
+Root records this transition only at the real paused/drained `5.5-adjudicate` owner request, after all109 native reports exist and before `repeat-1-collected.json` or `impact-repeat-1.json` exists. Preview writes nothing. Recording exclusively creates the immutable receipt and creation snapshots; root applies canonical sources and mirrors separately, under exact candidate hashes, before recording. The recorder checks the actual application again.
+
+The algorithm candidate must equal `pnpSourceCandidate(before)`: change the exact header ID and kind, then add `aliases: [def-ip-pnp-ista-with-denoiser]` immediately after kind. Every other byte, including the entire Definition/TikZ/references body, is preserved. Four fixed consumer item candidates and the fixed owning page may only replace literal old IDs with current IDs. Owning batch49 manifest, batch49 and merged contracts, and plan registry must be semantically identical except old/current identity, algorithm kind on the old-ID record, and citation quotes refreshed to the entire unchanged current Definition. No arbitrary metadata operation or proof repair is licensed. Frozen reader admissions stay unchanged.
+
+The existing FIRST mathematical report is bound as `root_math_review`, including its actual nonfatal native49 hash, minimal classification and exact four-consumer inventory. The separate `independent_review` must accept the complete finite carrier candidates by their before/after raw hashes. It has this exact schema:
+
+```json
+{
+  "accepted": true,
+  "reviewer_identity": "/root/INDEPENDENT_REVIEWER",
+  "current_review_granted": false,
+  "native_execution_coverage_adopted": false,
+  "before_source_sha256": "RAW_BEFORE",
+  "after_source_sha256": "RAW_AFTER",
+  "carrier_bindings": [{"path":"PATH","before_sha256":"RAW_BEFORE","after_sha256":"RAW_AFTER"}]
+}
+```
+
+This acceptance is distinct from native5.6 review. Root does not supply an independent review attributed to itself.
+
+## Request and commands
+
+Store every source/carrier preimage and candidate as regular nonsymlink files under `research/`. The request has:
+
+```js
+{
+ version:1, kind:'owner-pnp-classification-migration', run:RUN,
+ owner_identity:'/root', repairer_identity:'/root',
+ original_id:'def-ip-pnp-ista-with-denoiser', current_id:'alg-ip-pnp-ista-with-denoiser', batch:'49', home_page:'plug-and-play-mmse-regularization',
+ original_outcome:'confirmed_nonfatal', historical_only:true,
+ current_review_granted:false, native_execution_coverage_adopted:false,
+ entry:{before_source_file:'research/BEFORE.md',current_source_file:'research/AFTER.md',before_raw_sha256:SHA,after_raw_sha256:SHA},
+ carriers:[{path:LIVE_PATH,before_file:RESEARCH_PREIMAGE,current_file:RESEARCH_CANDIDATE}],
+ root_math_review:FIRST_REPORT, independent_review:EXACT_CANDIDATE_ACCEPTANCE,
+ consumer_ids:[/* the four IDs in PNP_CONSUMERS */]
+}
+```
+
+Do not supply creation snapshots, owner-request fields, bindings or payload SHA. The recorder derives them from actual runtime and files. It binds all109 original repeat reports/36 decisions, the331-verdict first Sol judge, unchanged baseline/Step4/initial pack, native49 immutable successful attempt/prompt/final log, the original batch21 receipts, the complete prior679-row certificate, candidate archives and explicit mathematical/independent acceptance. It preserves the judge ledger's original raw prefix while allowing ordinary later native appends.
+
+```sh
+node tools/step5-pnp-classification-migration.mjs preview --run RUN --authorization research/REQUEST.json
+# Root applies the exact source and mirror candidates, then:
+node tools/step5-pnp-classification-migration.mjs record --run RUN --authorization research/REQUEST.json
+node tools/step5-pnp-classification-migration.mjs check --run RUN
+```
+
+Only the root source application deletes the old canonical file. The receipt never changes baseline, frozen frontier/packs, native reports, prior certificates or judge history. Recording does not advance native runtime or assert collection, certification or gate success.
+
+## Native continuation and guards
+
+Collection authenticates the exact migration before validating old physical reviews against their historical source guards. It preserves the real old decision/review, separately attributes root classification repair, excludes old review credit, and emits five mandatory current review targets. The native5.6 pack binds this receipt/collection and assigns the algorithm and four consumers together, in supplier-first order, to one actual owner lane. Later repairs still trigger ordinary context invalidation and continuation.
+
+New certification requires actual successful native owner reports, immutable attempt results, exact assignments, prompt/final logs, current guards and supplier-interface review contexts for all five subjects. The old679-row certificate is readable only as its exact historical input; current closure rejects it. The projected algorithm cannot be a creation. Current Sol judgment is mandatory; a pre-migration judge cache is rejected. Protected deletion, selective judge policy, frontier gates and Step6 source selection, ownership, sealed deletion preimages and Git preflight all recognize only this authenticated pair, alongside the unchanged batch21 pair. Other deletions, alias substitutions and arbitrary renames remain forbidden.
+
+Focused tests run against the reviewed integration candidate:
+
+```sh
+node --test tools/step5-pnp-classification-migration.test.mjs tools/step5-pnp-classification-integration.test.mjs
+node --test tools/step5-pnp-classification-lifecycle.test.mjs
+node --test tools/step5-original-slot-reclassification.test.mjs tools/step6-original-slot-integration.test.mjs
+```
